## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to architect a secure, scalable incident-response automation platform across tenants using Azure AI services. Covers real-time event ingestion, strict data isolation, guardrails for safe prompt generation, canary testing, and comprehensive audit logging.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time Event Hubs ingestion with tenant-scoped event routing
- Tenant-isolated Cognitive Search indexes for grounded KB retrieval
- PII redaction via Text Analytics before processing and storage
- Canary playbook execution behind API Management with traffic splitting policies
- Data Lake for raw audit logs, Cosmos DB for structured remediation results
- Azure AD RBAC for multi-tenant access control

## Code Example
```javascript
// Initialize per-tenant Cognitive Search client with Managed Identity
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require('@azure/identity');
const { SearchIndexClient } = require('@azure/search-documents');

async function getTenantSearchClient(tenantId) {
  const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
  const indexName = `kb-${tenantId}`;
  return new SearchIndexClient(
    `https://${process.env.SEARCH_SERVICE}.search.windows.net/`,
    indexName,
    credential
  );
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
